    <details class="faq-item card" open>
        <summary><strong>Q: What is your primary area of specialization in cybersecurity?</strong></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>I specialize in <strong>Digital Forensics & Incident Response (DFIR)</strong>, <strong>SOC Operations</strong>, <strong>Network Security</strong>, and <strong>Linux Systems Hardening</strong>. My hands-on focus includes Splunk SIEM querying, Volatility memory analysis, Velociraptor hunting, and Cisco Network Defense.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item card">
        <summary><strong>Q: How do you build your home virtual lab?</strong></summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>My virtual lab runs on VirtualBox and VMware Workstation using an isolated host-only network. It includes Kali Linux, Security Onion, Splunk Enterprise, and a Windows 10 domain controller setup. Read my full <a href="/posts/home-lab-setup/">Home Lab Setup Guide</a> for exact hardware and configuration details.</p>
        </div>
    </details>

